# The tables of IDNA2008 for Unicode 17.0.0: which code points RFC 5892's
# derivation makes PVALID, and what its contextual rules and RFC 5893's Bidi
# rule read of a code point: its combining class, its script, its joining
# type and its bidirectional class.
#
# The tables are data, made and not typed: a one-off program applied RFC
# 5892's derivation (its section 3) to Python 3.15's `unicodedata`, whose
# `unidata_version` is 17.0.0, and to the Unicode Character Database 17.0.0's
# PropList, DerivedCoreProperties, HangulSyllableType, Scripts and
# DerivedJoiningType, on 2026-11-17, and wrote this module whole. Nothing here
# is edited by hand.

# The code points IDNA2008 (RFC 5892) makes PVALID, its exceptions included: pairs of first and last code point, in order.
